==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zigge]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 63% HP:
**1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 62% HP:
**1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 61% HP:
**1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns.
**1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 59% HP:
**1 [[Jackie Peng]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Peons head down the lane at a steady rate. You can farm them up and stall for a long time. When you attack the enemy base, the major threats start to roll out. However, since there is no boss shockwave, you can easily rush this stage with [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cat]]. Prepare your wallet for an all out-race with Giraffe Cat and make sure you save enough cash to protect your base from burrowing [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] as the Giraffes run past and destroy the base.

Alternatively, you can save up massive sums of money and create a stack of slow-moving, hard-hitting units ([[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cats]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cats]]) to take out the enemy base as the Pengs are spawning in. Be sure to meatshield frequently when using this strategy.

